HST Office: embedded spreadsheets and presentations are stored again; saving such a .docx no longer ends the office.

hst-format-names renamed the ClipboardFormat of the filter types calc8, calc8_template, impress8 and
impress8_template along with their display names ("Calc 8" -> "Sheets 8", "Impress 8" -> "Slides 8").
ClipboardFormat is not a display text: sfx2 matches it against the format names built into sot
(SotExchange, "Calc 8", "Impress 8") to find the filter of a storage from its MediaType
(SfxFilter::GetTypeFromStorage). With the renamed values no filter was found for an ODF spreadsheet or
presentation storage, so SfxBaseModel::storeToStorage failed for every embedded Calc or Impress object.
Writer then kept the object without its container (SwOLEObj::SetNode skips AssignToContainer when
InsertEmbeddedObject fails), and DocxAttributeOutput::WriteOLE dereferenced that null container: saving
a .docx with an embedded spreadsheet crashed (SIGSEGV, reported as signal 6 / exit 134) and the
document was not saved. The ClipboardFormat values go back to the upstream identifiers; the displayed
names (UIName) stay "Sheets 8" / "Slides 8".

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sfx2_misc (testOdfStorageTypeDetection); CppunitTest_sw_ooxmlexport4 (testEmbeddedXlsx),
CppunitTest_sw_ooxmlexport5 (testContentTypeOLE), CppunitTest_sw_ooxmlexport12 (testTdf122563).
